From: chasey-dev <ellenyoung0912@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] cfg80211: Recognize FT-EAP-SHA384 in AP RSNEs

cfg80211_ap_parse_rsn_ie() falls back to OPEN for AKM suite 13, so
hostapd's FT-EAP-SHA384 configuration loses its FT security type in the
driver. The suite now maps to the existing FT_WPA2_SHA384 flag, which
RSNE construction and station security selection already support.

Signed-off-by: chasey-dev <ellenyoung0912@gmail.com>
---
--- a/mt_wifi/os/linux/cfg80211/cfg80211_ap.c
+++ b/mt_wifi/os/linux/cfg80211/cfg80211_ap.c
@@ -3832,6 +3832,10 @@ BOOLEAN cfg80211_ap_parse_rsn_ie(
 					/* Set AP support WPA-PSK mode*/
 					SET_AKM_FT_WPA2PSK(sec_cfg->AKMMap);
 					break;
+				case 13:
+					/* Set AP support FT-EAP-SHA384 mode */
+					SET_AKM_FT_WPA2_SHA384(sec_cfg->AKMMap);
+					break;
 				case 25:
 					/*Set AP Support FT-SAE EXT AKM25*/
 					SET_AKM_FT_SAE_EXT(sec_cfg->AKMMap);
